# src/kernel_demos.manifest — the kernel PLUS its 25 module demonstrations
#
# Author: Manish Jagdish Thatte
# © Manish Jagdish Thatte
#
# The same 26 kernel modules as src/kernel.manifest, in the same order,
# followed by the 25 demo modules and a different entry point. HOSTED ONLY.
#
# WHY IT IS A SEPARATE MANIFEST AND NOT A FLAG. The T3 backend emits every
# function in the translation unit, reachable or not. With the demos beside the
# kernel the T3 code image reached **60,621 words against a 60,000-word
# ceiling** and the assembler refused it — the stack grows down from 60,000 and
# would have overwritten the code. Moving only the ENTRY POINT changed nothing,
# because reachability is not what that backend prunes on: the demos had to
# leave the translation unit entirely. Boot-only fits.
#
# So this is not "the kernel with demos switched on". It is a second program
# built from the same modules, and only one of the two has to fit on hardware.

# --- the kernel, exactly as src/kernel.manifest lists it --------------------
src/kernel/tmin2.mt
src/kernel/klog.mt
src/kernel/privilege.mt
src/security/capability.mt
src/kernel/panic.mt
src/kernel/guard.mt
src/kernel/context.mt
src/kernel/process.mt
src/kernel/scheduler.mt
src/kernel/timer.mt
src/kernel/signal.mt
src/kernel/interrupt.mt
src/mm/pgtable.mt
src/mm/vmem.mt
src/mm/mmu.mt
src/fs/inode.mt
src/fs/perms.mt
src/fs/fdtable.mt
src/fs/tritfs.mt

# HOSTED ONLY, and deliberately absent from src/kernel.manifest: it calls the
# fs_* builtins, which have no T3ISA syscall (`Undefined label: fs_mkdir`), so
# the kernel could not be built for its own target with it in. See the module
# header for the measurement.
src/fs/hosted_store.mt
src/ipc/messages.mt
src/ipc/pipe.mt
src/ipc/trit_stream.mt
src/drivers/tty.mt
src/syscall/syscall.mt
src/security/photon_cap.mt

# The kernel-side shell. In NEITHER manifest until 30 August 2026 (§4), so it
# was compiled by nothing; its `priv_name` had drifted from
# kernel/privilege.mt's because the flat namespace never made them meet.
src/userspace/shell.mt
src/boot.mt

# --- the demonstrations (src/demos/tmin2.mt also carries the expect_* helpers)
src/demos/tmin2.mt
src/demos/klog.mt
src/demos/privilege.mt
src/demos/panic.mt
src/demos/guard.mt
src/demos/context.mt
src/demos/process.mt
src/demos/scheduler.mt
src/demos/timer.mt
src/demos/signal.mt
src/demos/interrupt.mt
src/demos/pgtable.mt
src/demos/vmem.mt
src/demos/mmu.mt
src/demos/inode.mt
src/demos/perms.mt
src/demos/fdtable.mt
src/demos/tritfs.mt
src/demos/shell.mt
src/demos/messages.mt
src/demos/pipe.mt
src/demos/trit_stream.mt
src/demos/tty.mt
src/demos/syscall.mt
src/demos/capability.mt
src/demos/photon_cap.mt

# --- entry point ------------------------------------------------------------
src/entry_demos.mt
